<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Every customer-facing string of the payment UI, including the sentences that reach a
  merchant through UQPayError.message. Nothing in Kotlin may hardcode text a customer can
  read: it lives here so it can be translated without an API change, and so a reviewer can
  read the whole customer-visible vocabulary in one place.

  The SDK ships English only. A merchant who needs another language declares the same
  resource names in their own app under values-<language>/ — app resources win over library
  resources during merging, so an override needs no SDK release. This is documented in
  docs/integration-guide.md ("Localisation").

  Prefixed `uqpay_` because this is a library: resource names are merged into the host
  app's namespace, and an unprefixed `cancel` would collide with (or be silently overridden
  by) a merchant's own string of the same name. That prefix is also what makes the override
  above safe to write.
-->
