    <!--
      Amount fallback only. Amounts are normally rendered with the platform's currency
      formatter (see ui/AmountFormat.kt), which places the symbol, the grouping separators
      and the number of decimals according to the customer's locale and the currency —
      JPY has no decimals, and most of Europe does not use a dot. This pattern is used
      only when the currency code is one the platform cannot resolve, where printing the
      code beside the raw amount is the honest answer.
