    <!-- ==========================================================================
         UQPayError.message — one sentence per UQPayErrorCode.

         These are the sentences a merchant is invited to put in front of a customer,
         so each is written for a customer: it says what happened and, where there is
         one, what they can do about it. Anything a customer cannot act on — an
         uninitialised SDK, a rejected merchant token, a malformed request — deliberately
         reads as "we couldn't start this", because naming the merchant's bug to their
         customer helps nobody. The technical sentence for those lives in
         UQPayError.developerMessage, which is for logs and bug reports and must never be
         shown to a customer.

         Never tell a customer to "try again" for something retrying cannot fix. An
         authentication failure is the merchant's backend token, and inviting a retry
         loop there costs the customer their patience and the merchant the order.

         Wording is a compatibility concern in only one direction: a merchant may branch
         on UQPayErrorCode, never on the sentence. See docs/error-codes.md.
         ========================================================================== -->
    <string name="uqpay_error_not_initialized">This payment couldn\'t be started. Please contact the store for help.</string>
    <string name="uqpay_error_invalid_configuration">This payment couldn\'t be started. Please contact the store for help.</string>
    <string name="uqpay_error_invalid_request">This payment couldn\'t be started. Please contact the store for help.</string>
    <string name="uqpay_error_invalid_payment_method">That payment method cannot be used for this payment.</string>
    <string name="uqpay_error_network">The payment could not be completed because of a connection problem.</string>
    <string name="uqpay_error_timeout">We are still waiting for confirmation of this payment.</string>
    <string name="uqpay_error_authentication_failed">This payment couldn\'t be completed. Please contact the store for help.</string>
